{
 "summary": "Routes all block script checking in ConnectBlock through CCheckQueue regardless of thread count, eliminating the dedicated inline execution branch for single-threaded validation. It extracts helper functions EnsureTxData and GetScriptCacheEntry, and strips CheckInputScripts of its pvChecks and CheckInputScriptsFor parameters so it is used exclusively for inline mempool checks. It also ensures the script execution cache is populated during TestBlockValidity regardless of whether checkqueue worker threads are present.",
 "problem": "CheckInputScripts had confusing dual behavior: executing scripts inline if pvChecks was null, or appending CScriptCheck objects to a vector if pvChecks was provided. Because script execution cache insertion was guarded with !pvChecks, multithreaded script checks in TestBlockValidity never populated the script execution cache.",
 "evidence": [
  "Commit 496ed47a80: \"Previously, script execution cache population during TestBlockValidity (fJustCheck=true) only worked in the single-threaded case, because CheckInputScripts guarded the cache insertion with !pvChecks. In the multithreaded case, pvChecks was always set, so the cache was never populated.\"",
  "PR description: \"CheckInputScripts currently only does what its name implies if there is no multithreading usage for validation... This dual use makes the function hard to grasp and its naming confusing.\""
 ],
 "dependencies": {
