 },
 "scope_notes": "Touches core consensus validation and block connection logic in ConnectBlock and CheckInputScripts. Encapsulates m_script_execution_cache access methods inside ValidationCache.",
 "changed_since_previous": "Encapsulated m_script_execution_cache inside ValidationCache (exposing IsScriptValidated and CacheScriptValidation), and removed the CheckInputScriptsFor enum now that only the mempool calls CheckInputScripts.",
 "card": "ConnectBlock is updated to route all block script validation through CCheckQueue, eliminating a dedicated single-threaded verification branch since CCheckQueue executes checks synchronously on the calling thread when no worker threads exist. CheckInputScripts is stripped of its pvChecks and CheckInputScriptsFor parameters and now only executes scripts inline for mempool acceptance, while ConnectBlock constructs script checks directly. The refactor also resolves a long-standing omission where block script validation results during TestBlockValidity were never added to the cache in multithreaded mode. ValidationCache now encapsulates access to the script execution cache with explicit query and insertion methods. The author states this clean-up prepares the validation pipeline for batch validation work.",
